SCOPE

Apache-2.0 (open source):

  src/Pix3.Rooms.Protocol/    the wire contract     — see its own LICENSE
  tools/Pix3.Rooms.LoadGen/   reference bot client  — see its own LICENSE
  docs/protocol.md            the byte-exact protocol specification
  docs/protocol-vectors.json  the golden wire vectors

Commercial (this licence):

  src/Pix3.Rooms.Server/      the Room Fabric server implementation
  tests/                      its test suite
  deploy/                     deployment configuration

The split is deliberate. The protocol is an interface, not the product: a
complete, independent client implementation of it already ships inside
`@pix3/runtime` under Apache-2.0, together with the same golden vectors. Anyone
may implement this protocol, on either side of the wire, including a competing
server. What is licensed commercially is *this* server implementation — its room
lifecycle, area-of-interest replication, quotas, multi-tenancy and operations.

